{"entity": "Allah", "type": "person", "description": "Allah is described as the one true God, the central divine entity who is the foundation of a strong relationship with believers. His character is characterized by glory, mercy, compassion, truth, holiness, goodness, and love. Allah is also portrayed as omniscient, omnipotent, and sovereign over all creation, being transcendent and beyond human understanding, yet in control of everything. He is the true Creator and the ultimate object of worship and trust.\n\nThe descriptions highlight Allah's desire for closeness with humanity, noting that He interacts with people in different ways across time and invites them into a covenant relationship. Believers are called to obey His commands as an act of love, recognizing that Allah Himself first loved humanity. While Allah is infinitely greater than human comprehension, He is worthy of praise and is presented as the Father who loves and the divine being with whom humans have a relationship. Some descriptions also mention alternative names like Elohim and Yahweh, which describe different aspects of His being. Furthermore, Allah is said to have a clear and beautiful image that is important for deepening one's relationship with Him."}
