{"entity": "Yesus", "type": "person", "description": "Yesus is a central figure presented as the Son of God and the ultimate revelation of God, sent into the world to demonstrate God's perfect character and to provide salvation. His life and atoning death are considered key to understanding God's love and the Father. Yesus is seen as the answer to knowing God and deepening a relationship with Him, offering a generous exchange and urging repentance.\n\nHe is depicted as the Savior and Redeemer, offering solutions and describing the spiritual condition of believers. Yesus overcame sin and its punishment, and His teachings emphasize abiding in Him, obeying Him, and remaining in His love. He is also mentioned in the context of correcting misconceptions about Allah. His role is to offer salvation and foster a close relationship with humanity."}
